codex
I found explicit counterexamples to two printed claims: a pure section can evaluate to zero modulo both primes, and \(F_{51}\) has a nonzero binary section that vanishes at every scalar, although 51 is not Carmichael. The balanced odd-semiprime version of C4 still appears correct. The finite-difference window also survives, but its zero predicate is nonmonotone, so it is not the factorial prefix predicate.

